The command first appeared in the WIDE  Hydrangea  IPv6  protocol
stack kit.  There used to be some text that recommended users not
to  let  advertise  Router  Advertisement messages on an upstream
link to avoid undesirable redirect messages.  However,  based  on
later  discussion  in  the  IETF  IPng working group, all routers
should rather advertise the messages regardless  of  the  network
topology, in order to ensure reachability.
